      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T05:46:37Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Thanks for the clarification. After tracing the control flow, I found that the early return at line 241 checks the result of verifying image-bmc only.\n\nIf image-bmc is absent, verification falls back to the individual BMC partitions. A partition signature failure makes checkAndVerifyImage() return false, but Signature::verify() does not immediately return false after this second call.\n\nFor example, modifying the kernel contents while keeping its original signature leaves bmcFilesFound\u003dtrue and valid\u003dfalse. Full-image verification can still succeed because it verifies the concatenated signature files, which remain unchanged. With no optional images present, execution then reaches the final assertion.\n\nWhen assertions are enabled, the old code aborts on this path; when disabled through NDEBUG, it falls through to return true. The explicit check intentionally rejects the image in both configurations.\n\nAdded debug traces to record the full-image and partition verification results, along with regression coverage. All 9 signature tests passed with signature verification enabled.",
      "parentUuid": "09ff4586_1eba4ce7",
      "revId": "2af71da7ad4d78a79ce69b603f3489c4c411761f",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
